TempleOS notices and third-party provenance
============================================

TempleOS was written by Terry A. Davis and released as public domain. The
project's original credits are preserved in docs/templeos/credits.dd. This file
summarizes the material called out there and the dependency added by this
repository; it does not replace notices embedded in individual files.

Separately licensed or public-domain material
----------------------------------------------

* deps/holylua is a Git submodule derived from Lua. The upstream Lua source is
  Copyright (C) 1994-2026 Lua.org, PUC-Rio and is distributed under the Lua
  license reproduced in deps/holylua/LICENSE. Copies staged into generated
  images remain subject to that license.

* src/kernel/font_std.hc is credited to FreeDOS and identified as public
  domain by the original TempleOS credits.

* src/misc/bible.txt is Project Gutenberg Etext #10, The King James Bible.
  Its complete historical notice is preserved at the beginning of that file.
  It identifies the text as public domain in the United States and specifies
  conditions for distribution under the PROJECT GUTENBERG trademark.

* Webster's Dictionary data used by the autocomplete system is credited to
  Project Gutenberg in the original TempleOS credits.

* Mountain and wolf graphics used by TempleOS games are credited as derived
  from public-domain-photos.com and identified as public domain by the
  original TempleOS credits.

Materials with unresolved permission or licensing
-------------------------------------------------

The public-domain notice in LICENSE does not grant rights to the following
third-party material. The repository does not contain enough evidence to
establish redistribution permission or complete license terms:

* src/kernel/font_cyrillic.hc is credited to an Orient Display image. The
  original TempleOS credits explicitly say it was used without permission.

* src/misc/pci_devices.dd is credited to pcidatabase.com; no license is
  recorded in the repository.

* src/demo/tohtmltotxtdemo/to_html.hc credits an unidentified author of
  CppHtml; no license is recorded in the repository.

* src/adam/a_math_ode.hc is described as adapted from Numerical Recipes in C;
  no permission or license for that adaptation is recorded here.

* src/kernel/mem/m_alloc_free.hc and src/kernel/compress.hc are described as
  based on an algorithm seen at Ticketmaster and an unspecified magazine,
  respectively; the precise sources and terms are not recorded.

* Some game art was commissioned from Cody Rigby, but the repository does not
  record the applicable copyright assignment or license.

* The credits mention ATA definitions originally taken from Linux, shell
  scripts by Erik van der Karbargenbok, and other code or technical material
  found in documentation or on the internet. Exact source versions and terms
  are not recorded.

Historical bootstrap files under bootstrap/ reproduce earlier TempleOS
artifacts and may contain the same materials and provenance described above.
Resolve the items in this section before relying on the repository for a
redistribution that requires complete third-party rights clearance.
